Two files, one block: 13 new rules in public/style.css, all scoped to #settings-panel-board and kept at
class weight with :where(), and two attributes on the add-folder input in public/index.html (a shorter
placeholder and the full sentence in its title). public/app.js, lib/ and server.js are untouched, and the
markup the roots rows are drawn from (app.js paintScanRoots) did not change - only what the CSS does with it.

Change 1 of 2 - the roots read as one control group
  what moved: .settings-roots becomes a column of cards (4 px between them, 6 px above), and .settings-root
    becomes a 28 px card: surface fill, 1 px line, 6 px radius, 8 px left padding, and a uniform 8 px gap
    between its path, its state chip and its remove control. The path takes the row's slack (flex: 1 with
    min-width: 0) and ellipsizes a path longer than that, with the full path kept in the markup's title;
    the chip becomes a 10 px pill (the existing .bad variant gets a red border and fill); the ✕ becomes a
    real 24x24 button with a hover fill instead of an unstyled UA button.
  asked by: "The 'Folders the board scans' block must read as one control group: a visible gap between each
    root's path, its state chip and its remove control" - the target sentence in
    ledger/gui-improve/baseline/README.md ("The surface") and capture.json surface.change.
  measured: path -> chip 0 -> 8 px; chip -> ✕ 3.84 -> 8 px; card height 28 -> 28 px (unchanged); ✕
    31.8 x 28 -> 24 x 24 (the UA button's width had no relation to its glyph; 24 x 24 is the deliberate
    target, and the title still names the folder). Identical at 1440x900, 1280x800 and 1024x768.

Change 2 of 2 - the add row uses the width it has left, so its hint is readable
  what moved: .settings-roots-add becomes a flex row (6 px gap, 6 px above) whose input takes the remaining
    width (flex: 1, min-width: 0) at 26 px tall and 11.5 px mono, with the button 26 px tall and flush to
    row's right edge. The placeholder is shortened in public/index.html from "an absolute folder path
    - e.g. the parent of your projects" to "an absolute folder path", and the full sentence is carried in
    the input's title ("an absolute folder path, e.g. the parent of your projects. Enter adds it"), so the
    example stays discoverable without competing with the field for width.
  asked by: "and the add-folder field given the width its row has left so its hint is readable" - the same
    target sentence, its second clause.
  measured: input 154 -> 223.52 px (client 222) of the 310 px row; button 78.375 -> 80.48 px; space right
    of the button 73.78 -> 0.00 px; the hint 382.66 px at the input's 12 px mono -> 145.42 px at 11.5 px,
    inside the field's 222 px, so it paints whole (before: "an absolute folder pat"). The width alone could
    not make the hint readable - 382.66 px does not fit even the whole 310 px row - so the hint was cut to
    what the row can show and the rest kept in `title`. Identical at all three viewports.

A consequence, not a third change: the Board panel's content is 14 px taller (scrollHeight 1599 -> 1613):
6 px above the cards, 4 px between them and 6 px above the add row, less 2 px because the add row is 26 px
tall where the unstyled row was 28 (button 78.38 x 28 -> 80.48 x 26, input 154 x 20 -> 223.52 x 26). The
Settings window still opens at 340 x 520 with the block's title, both cards and the add row in view; no
other row's own layout changed, and the rows below it sit 14 px lower.

The search state is unchanged: filling #settings-search with "flash" still hides the whole block
(display: none on .settings-roots and .settings-roots-add), and clearing it restores the flex rows. Every
selector is wrapped in :where() so these `display` declarations stay at class weight and the filter's
`.settings-group .search-hidden { display: none }` still wins while the query is live.

Verified with a Playwright Chromium probe against this tree served on 127.0.0.1:7493 with a scratch config
whose scanRoots are C:/CodeReviews and C:/sefl-mvn-local (the baseline's two), at the baseline's three
viewports and its `open` and `search` states; the numbers above are that run's, and the surface shots of
the applied tree were read to confirm the block paints as one group. The compare stage owns the final
after set and the comparison page.

